On Fri, 2015-04-24 at 08:58 +0200, Iosu Paradinas wrote:

> However I thought that the scaling parameter would be Z in one model
> and 1/Z in the other. Isn´t it? In such case, shouldn´t the fit of
> both models be *equal*?

yes, this is likely the issue. since the prior is defined for the
scaling, beta, where you have

	z1
	z2 = beta*z1

or you have

	z2
	z1 = z2/beta

since the prior for beta and 1/beta is not the same, it will give
different marginal likelihood, DIC++

